    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="040e624a-c81d-542f-84ee-db4c4eb1d6df" activityNameId="0ce7b706-021d-5764-848c-76dc414141f6" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Slurry store and processing</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Slurry store and processing
The module includes a covered, underfloor and rectangular slurry store made of concrete. Also included is a marine screw agitator. Size: 300 m3. Lifetime of the building is 40 years.;
UUID: 9d70a998-fafe-393c-8056-75172bab8273
The inventory takes into account the use of construction materials and building machines for construction, repair and replacement including waste disposal and the transportation of the materials to the building site. Not taken into account were direct emission of the construction, disposal of production waste and the use of resources during utilization phase. 
Location: &lt;null&gt;
Technology: The data of the inventory are based on one example of a typical agricultural building.
Time period: undefined
Production volume: Existing slurry store volume in CH in 1996: 14'847'685 m3.
Sampling: The inventory is calculated based on a solid database of agricultural buildings. 
Extrapolations: &lt;null&gt;
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_9d70a998-fafe-393c-8056-75172bab8273.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
